\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You're right - I moved too quickly to the "correct" interpretation without sitting in the ambiguity the audience would experience. Let me reconsider what possibilities would be alive for them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <notes> The audience hearing verses 3-10 has multiple interpretive paths available, and the riddle form deliberately keeps these open. The rhetorical power comes partly from which interpretation they commit to before the reveal. </notes>\
