When you said Zedekiah had a third option (turning to the LORD), I immediately accepted this reframed the entire riddle. But we didn't establish from Ezekiel 17 itself that this option existed. 2 Chronicles mentions it, but Ezekiel 17 presents a binary: stay loyal to Babylon or turn to Egypt. The "third way" might be reading backwards from other texts rather than finding it here.\

\b Insufficient Evidence:
\b0 \
We both treated the "trees of the field" (verse 24) as certainly meaning "nations" without adequate justification. The immediate context is agricultural. While trees-as-nations appears elsewhere in scripture, we needed to demonstrate why that reading is necessary here rather than simply possible.\
Our claim that the dual framework (political events ARE theological events) operates throughout the chapter actually only has strong evidence for the oath specifically. We extrapolated a general principle from a specific case involving YHWH's name.\

\b What We Left Out:
