\b Unsubstantiated Claims That Matter:
\b0 \
My assertion that divine sovereignty is "always relevant" for AI went far beyond available evidence. Ezekiel 17 shows it was relevant for Zedekiah under specific covenant conditions. The jump to "always" wasn't warranted.\
We connected this passage to messianic hope (Isaiah 11, the eternal Davidic promise) based on plausible but not conclusive parallels. The tender sprig could be about dynastic restoration without being specifically messianic. We treated interpretive possibility as certainty.\
