Many chapters of Ezekiel very much address the accusation that the LORD abandoned his people, sometimes in advance of the accusation. Having multiple oracles from multiple perspectives allows the book of Ezekiel as a whole to address the multiple reasons real people do things. The question is what false beliefs Ezekiel 17 is positioning itself to answer. Do you see evidence of targeting the abandonment false narrative in Ezekiel 17? Possibly by reference to earlier chapters which dealt with that narrative more directly? If so, we will need to work that into our picture of what the chapter is doing.\
